  "name": "Zurkhaneh (morshed chant for varzesh-e pahlavani)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Iranian zurkhaneh, the traditional gymnasium where athletes perform the ritual exercises of varzesh-e pahlavani in a sunken pit. From a raised seat the morshed beats a large goblet drum, the zarb, and rings a bell to honour arriving champions and mark transitions, chanting verses from Ferdowsi's Shahnameh, mystical poetry and praises of the Prophet and Imam Ali in rhythms matched to each exercise; UNESCO has inscribed the Pahlevani and Zoorkhanei rituals on its Representative List. The tombak card stands in for the zarb.",
  "recipe": "classic modern zurkhaneh, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. tombak. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
